(Regression test found while fixing bug #44. A `{name}` whose name is
 QUOTED - `{'the running total'}` - and a bare list literal `{[1, 2]}` do
 not parse as variable parts at all: they parse as EXPRESSIONS. Print's
 expression arm had a Map case from stage 1e2 but never a List one, so
 both spellings printed the list's heap address even in Print position -
 the one position bug #44 reported as working.

 Fixing the other sinks without this would have inverted the bug: every
 sink but Print would render a quoted list name correctly.

 Acceptance: a quoted name, a list literal and a nested literal render the
 same in Print position as they do captured into a text - and a map, which
 already worked, still does.)

a list called 'the running total' is [1, 2, 3].
a map called 'the record' is {"name": "Ada"}.

Print "{'the running total'}".
a text called 'the quoted name' is "{'the running total'}".
Print 'the quoted name'.

Print "{[7, 8]}".
a text called 'the literal' is "{[7, 8]}".
Print 'the literal'.

Print "{[[1], [2, 3]]}".
a text called 'the nested literal' is "{[[1], [2, 3]]}".
Print 'the nested literal'.

Print "{'the record'}".
a text called 'the quoted map' is "{'the record'}".
Print 'the quoted map'.
